  designNotes: "2026-08-28, explicit user request (\u52A0\u5165 Meshy_AI_Parkside_Portrait_biped
    (9).zip \u7684 Double_Combo_Attack) - clip 'Wushi_DoubleCombo' ('Scene' take,
    without_skin FBX 206KB, 85 frames / 2.833s). A genuine two-hit downward combo
    - UNLIKE the two removed Meshy attacks (AdvancingCuts / LungeSlash), both swings
    here actually sweep DOWN through the PlayerHurtbox height at speed with real
    forward reach. Measured offline via AnimationMode.SampleAnimationClip retargeted
    onto the live 4x \u6B66\u58EB (same methodology as SwordJudgment / OverheadSlam),
    reading BladeHitbox world Y + speed + blade-forward-of-hips (chest.forward):\n 
    - Hit 1 (nt 0.23-0.31): blade crashes Y 4.32 -> 1.22 -> 0.52 across nt 0.23-0.27,
    speed peak 72 u/s at nt 0.25, blade 2.0-2.4 units forward of body core at contact
    - clean diagonal downcut through the hurtbox.\n  - Hit 2 (nt 0.60-0.66): blade
    descends Y 4.54 -> 2.07 -> 0.68 across nt 0.61-0.65, speed peak 45 u/s, blade
    ~1.9 units forward at the nt 0.62-0.64 contact (retracts toward the body by nt
    0.67). damageMultiplier 1.15 (the committed second hit).\n\nLive in-Play test
    (frames WERE advancing this time): hit 1 landed exactly -14 on a glued Player
    at 1.8 units (nt ~0.27, dead in the window) - BUT connection is marginal: at
    2.0+ units without root motion it whiffed, and even at 1.7 one run registered
    nothing. The clip is authored so the character STARTS ~3 units behind its root
    and walks FORWARD to it over the combo; with useRootMotion=0 the visible body
    (and blade) lags behind the boss's actual position, so the reach the offline
    hips-relative numbers imply is not all there at the boss's real transform. Compromise
    for this first pass: maxDistance 2.5 (down from 3.3) so the boss only commits
    to it when close enough that hit 1 has a real chance. If it still whiffs a lot
    in real play, OR reads as 'no lunge' (the LungeSlash feedback), the proper fix
    is useRootMotion=1 - which in a quick test (window 0-0.55, distance 2.2) DID
    make both hits land (-46) - PLUS clearing _currentAttack when LeapSlam/Breakdance
    interrupt an attack (CHANGELOG's flagged 'root-motion attack trap'); left for
    a follow-up rather than done blind here.\n\n2026-08-28, \u4F7F\u7528\u8005\u8981\u6C42
    \"\u5927\u62DB\u4EE5\u5916\u7684\u653B\u64CA\u56FA\u5B9A\u6263 5%\" \u4E14 \"\u4E0D\u8981\u786C\u7DE8\u78BC\u8840\u91CF
    \u800C\u662F\u767E\u5206\u6BD4\u8A2D\u5B9A\" - healthDamageIsPercentOfTargetMax=true,
    baseHealthDamage=5 (read as 5% of the hit target's Health.MaxHealth, resolved
    in BossHitbox at hit time - not a baked 25). Both hit windows' damageMultiplier
    normalised to 1 (2nd was 1.15) so every hit is exactly 5%. Note: 2 windows =>
    both landing = 10% total; if the user wants the whole ATTACK capped at 5%, drop
    a window or set baseHealthDamage 2.5.\n\nTuning (health 5% of max per hit, poise
    12, knockback 3, cooldown 2.8s, non-major, no derive) sits mid-pool. No derivation
    wired - keep it self-contained for the first pass. keepOriginalPositionY=true
    on the clip import (the AdvancingCuts sink lesson) - BakeMesh sweep in Play confirmed
    lowest mesh vertex stays 0.64-0.67, above ground ~0.5, no sinking."
